Let $y=\left(\frac{1}{x}\right)^{2 x}\begin{aligned}
& \ell \text { ny }=2 x \ell n\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) \\
& \ell \text { ny }=-2 x \ell \ln x \\
& \frac{1}{y} \frac{d y}{d x}=-2(1+\ell n x)
\end{aligned}$
for $\mathrm{x} \gt \frac{1}{\mathrm{e}} \mathrm{f}^{\mathrm{n}}$ is decreasing
