\end{aligned}$

$(E m f)_{\text {induced }}=-L \frac{d i}{d t}$<br  />In magnitude form,
$\begin{aligned}
& \left|\operatorname{Emf}_{\text {ind }}\right|=\left|(-) L \frac{\mathrm{di}}{\mathrm{dt}}\right| \\
& \Rightarrow 0.1=\frac{(\mathrm{L})[+2-(-2)]}{0.2} \\
& \Rightarrow \mathrm{L}=\frac{0.1 \times 0.2}{4}=5 \mathrm{mH}
\end{aligned}$

The difference in frequency in open organ pipe $=\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{f}=\frac{\mathrm{nv}}{2 \mathrm{~L}} \\
& \Delta \mathrm{f}=\frac{6 \mathrm{v}}{2 \times 0.6}-\frac{5 \mathrm{v}}{2 \times 0.9} \\
& \mathrm{v}=333 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s} \\
& \Delta \mathrm{f}=740 \mathrm{~Hz}
\end{aligned}$
